        "original_id": "90bfab9b-12b8-50e0-89db-4fdf47371098",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Genera: Tritonia, Phyteuma, Zygotritonia\n- Plants: flowering plants\n- Families: iris family, Campanulaceae\n- Places: Europe, Morocco\n- Concepts: genus etymology, zygomorphic\n\nFacts:\n- Tritonia is a genus of flowering plants in the iris family that was first described as a genus in 1802.\n- Phyteuma is a genus of flowering plants in the family Campanulaceae that is native to Europe and Morocco.\n- The genus name Zygotritonia is derived from the word zygomorphic, meaning bilabiate, and from its apparent resemblance to some species in the genus Tritonia.",
